# Canonicalise on the apex. <link rel="canonical"> already points there, and a
# www copy that also answers 200 splits ranking signals between two hostnames.
https://www.schoolstack.ai/*    https://schoolstack.ai/:splat    301!

# Outbound CTA instrumentation.
#
# Netlify Analytics is built from CDN request logs, so it can only ever see
# requests to this domain. Every tool CTA points off-site, which means clicking
# "Open Space" is invisible to it - the one number worth having. Routing those
# clicks through /go/* makes each one a logged first-party request.
#
# 302, deliberately, NOT 301: a 301 is cached by the browser, so the second and
# every later click never reaches the CDN and never gets counted. 302 keeps
# every click observable. robots.txt disallows /go/ so crawlers do not inflate it.
/go/space          https://space.schoolstack.ai          302
/go/budget         https://budget.schoolstack.ai         302
/go/access         https://access.schoolstack.ai         302
# Lending Lab is not promoted on schoolstack.ai while it gets more work, so
# nothing on the site links these two. They stay so that links already shared
# (emails, decks) keep working; tools/verify-render.mjs lists them as the only
# rules allowed to have no CTA on the page.
/go/lending-lab    https://www.lendinglab.org            302
/go/screener       https://www.lendinglab.org/screener   302

# Clean URLs for the other pages. Netlify already serves about.html at
# /about (and so on); these state it rather than relying on the default.
/about             /about.html                           200
/privacy           /privacy.html                         200
/terms             /terms.html                           200
